  "question": {
    "text": "<p>One mole of an ideal gas expands adiabatically from an initial state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> to final state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>. Another mole of the same gas expands isothermally from a different initial state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math> to the same final state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>. The ratio of the specific heats at constant pressure and constant volume of this ideal gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math>. What is the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></math>?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>&#947;</mi></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As we know for an Adiabatic process</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>Constant</mtext></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0006_168e088c65b6.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 294px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>For Isothermal process</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Dividing equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
